                <rect x="78" y="30" width="10" height="7" rx="2"/><rect x="92" y="30" width="10" height="7" rx="2"/>
                <rect x="106" y="30" width="10" height="7" rx="2"/>
                <rect x="30" y="41" width="70" height="7" rx="2"/>
              </g>
              <g class="buddy__eyes"><circle cx="52" cy="18" r="4"/><circle cx="78" cy="18" r="4"/></g>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <span class="buddy__name">Keyboard</span>
        </div>
        <div class="buddy buddy--headphones">
          <div class="buddy__hop">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 100 92" aria-hidden="true">
              <path class="buddy__band buddy__band--edge" d="M19 56V46a31 31 0 0 1 62 0v10"/>
              <path class="buddy__band" d="M19 56V46a31 31 0 0 1 62 0v10"/>
              <rect class="buddy__shape" x="5" y="48" width="28" height="38" rx="11"/>
              <rect class="buddy__shape" x="67" y="48" width="28" height="38" rx="11"/>
              <g class="buddy__eyes"><circle cx="19" cy="63" r="4.2"/><circle cx="81" cy="63" r="4.2"/></g>
              <circle class="buddy__blush" cx="19" cy="75" r="4"/><circle class="buddy__blush" cx="81" cy="75" r="4"/>
            </svg>
            <span class="notes" aria-hidden="true"><i>♪</i><i>♫</i></span>
          </div>
          <span class="buddy__name">Headphones</span>
        </div>

        <div class="bubble" aria-hidden="true">connected!</div>

        <button class="kvm" type="button" data-kvm aria-label="Press the KVM switch">
          <span class="kvm__led kvm__led--mac"></span>
          <span class="kvm__button"></span>
          <span class="kvm__led kvm__led--pc"></span>
          <span class="kvm__label">KVM</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <figcaption>
        <span class="demo__hint">Go on, press the KVM button.</span>
        <span class="demo__status" data-status aria-live="polite">Your devices are with the Mac.</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- How it works ---------- #}
<section class="section section--tint" id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2>You switch. AutoSwitch does the rest.</h2>
      <p class="section__lead">
        A KVM switch shares one desk between two computers. Wired things follow it; Bluetooth
        things stay behind. AutoSwitch runs quietly on both computers and closes that gap.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="flow">
      <li>
        <span class="flow__icon"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="8" width="18" height="9" rx="3"/><circle cx="12" cy="12.5" r="2.2"/><path d="M7 12.5h.01M17 12.5h.01"/></svg></span>
        <h3>You press the KVM button</h3>
        <p>Like always. The KVM moves your screen and USB devices to the other computer.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="flow__icon"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="6"/><path d="m20 20-4.5-4.5"/></svg></span>
        <h3>AutoSwitch notices</h3>
        <p>It watches the USB hub inside your KVM, so each computer knows whether it was picked.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="flow__icon"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 12h13m0 0-4-4m4 4-4 4"/><path d="M20 6v12"/></svg></span>
        <h3>Your Bluetooth devices follow</h3>
        <p>The computer you leave lets go, the one you picked takes over. A few seconds, nothing to click.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="compare">
      <div class="compare__side compare__side--before">
        <h3>Without it, every switch</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Open Bluetooth settings</li>
          <li>Forget the trackpad</li>
          <li>Pair it on the other computer</li>
          <li>Press the channel key on the keyboard, reconnect the headphones…</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="compare__side compare__side--after">
        <h3>With AutoSwitch</h3>
        <p class="compare__big">Press the KVM button.</p>
        <p>That's it. A small panel shows each device arriving, then gets out of the way.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Works with ---------- #}
<section class="section" id="works">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Works with</p>
      <h2>The devices on your desk</h2>
      <p class="section__lead">Each kind of device switches its own way. AutoSwitch knows which, and does the right thing.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="devices">
      <li class="device">
        <svg class="device__icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 48 48"><rect x="7" y="9" width="34" height="30" rx="6"/><path d="M7 31h34"/></svg>
        <h3>Apple Magic Trackpad, Keyboard &amp; Mouse</h3>
        <p>They pair with one computer at a time. AutoSwitch unpairs on the way out and pairs on the way in.</p>
        <p class="device__os"><span>Mac ✓</span><span>Windows ✓</span></p>
      </li>
      <li class="device">
        <svg class="device__icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 48 48"><rect x="4" y="15" width="40" height="20" rx="5"/><path d="M11 22h0M17 22h0M23 22h0M29 22h0M35 22h0M14 28h20"/><path d="M33 6l4 4-4 4M37 10H27"/></svg>
        <h3>Logitech Easy-Switch</h3>
        <p>K380, MX keyboards and mice keep a channel per computer. AutoSwitch tells them to hop to the other one.</p>
        <p class="device__os"><span>Mac ✓</span><span>Windows ✓</span></p>
      </li>
      <li class="device">
        <svg class="device__icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 48 48"><rect x="4" y="15" width="40" height="20" rx="5"/><path d="M11 22h0M17 22h0M23 22h0M29 22h0M35 22h0M14 28h20"/><path d="M18 9l6-4 6 4"/></svg>
        <h3>ZMK keyboards</h3>
        <p>With the free <a href="https://github.com/casab/zmk-autoswitch">zmk-autoswitch</a> module, their Bluetooth profiles switch the same way.</p>
        <p class="device__os"><span>Mac ✓</span><span>Windows ✓</span></p>
      </li>
      <li class="device">
        <svg class="device__icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 48 48"><path d="M9 30v-6a15 15 0 0 1 30 0v6"/><rect x="6" y="28" width="8" height="12" rx="3"/><rect x="34" y="28" width="8" height="12" rx="3"/></svg>
        <h3>Headphones &amp; speakers</h3>
        <p>Most join whichever computer asks. AutoSwitch disconnects them on one and connects them on the other.</p>
        <p class="device__os"><span>Mac ✓</span><span>Windows ✓</span></p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="devices__more">
      Game controllers, other keyboards? AutoSwitch tells you what's possible for each device.
      <a href="/devices/">See the device guide →</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Set up ---------- #}
<section class="section section--tint" id="setup">
  <div class="wrap setup">
    <div class="setup__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Set up</p>
      <h2>Two minutes, once</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <span class="steps__badge">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Install it on both computers</h3>
            <p>The computer you leave lets go of your devices, so the other one can take them.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="steps__badge">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Show it your KVM</h3>
            <p>Press <em>Learn</em>, then switch the KVM away and back. AutoSwitch spots the USB device that comes and goes.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="steps__badge">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Add your devices</h3>
            <p>Pick them from the list. AutoSwitch tells you how each one switches and sets it up to match.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="shots">
      <figure class="shot">
        <img src="/assets/img/mac-panel.png" alt="AutoSwitch KVM in the macOS menu bar: three devices, two connected, one connecting" width="300" height="319" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>Mac: in the menu bar</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="shot">
        <img src="/assets/img/windows-panel.png" alt="AutoSwitch KVM in the Windows tray: three devices, two connected, one connecting" width="312" height="323" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption>Windows: in the tray</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Features ---------- #}
<section class="section" id="features">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The good stuff</p>
      <h2>Small app, big sigh of relief</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="features">
      <li>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="4" y="5" width="16" height="12" rx="3"/><path d="M8 10h8M8 13h5M9 21h6"/></svg>
        <div><h3>Tells you, quietly</h3><p>A small panel shows each device arriving, then hides. No pings, no pile of notifications.</p></div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 18h14M7 14h10M9 10h6M11 6h2"/></svg>
        <div><h3>The whole desk at once</h3><p>Keyboard, mouse, trackpad, headphones, with profiles like "Desk" and "Travel".</p></div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M7 11V7a2 2 0 1 1 4 0v4m0-1V5a2 2 0 1 1 4 0v6m0-2a2 2 0 1 1 4 0v4a7 7 0 0 1-14 0v-2a2 2 0 1 1 4 0"/></svg>
        <div><h3>Respects your hands</h3><p>Switched a keyboard yourself with its own key? AutoSwitch leaves it where you put it.</p></div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M20 14.5A8 8 0 0 1 9.5 4a8 8 0 1 0 10.5 10.5z"/></svg>
        <div><h3>Naps when you nap</h3><p>Devices are released when the computer sleeps. A sleeping keyboard never holds up the rest.</p></div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 5v14M15 5v14"/></svg>
        <div><h3>Pause any time</h3><p>One click to pause, Connect all and Release all buttons, optional keyboard shortcuts.</p></div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3l7 3v6c0 4.5-3 7.5-7 9-4-1.5-7-4.5-7-9V6z"/></svg>
        <div><h3>Minds its own business</h3><p>No account, no analytics. It only talks to GitHub, to check for updates, which install themselves.</p></div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Download ---------- #}
<section class="section section--tint" id="download">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Download</p>
      <h2>Free, for both of your computers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="downloads">
      <article class="dl">
        <h3>macOS</h3>
        <p class="dl__req">macOS 13 Ventura or later · Apple silicon &amp; Intel</p>
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ site.download.mac }}">
          <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0-5-5m5 5 5-5M5 21h14"/></svg>
          Download for Mac
        </a>
        <p class="dl__note">
          Open the DMG and drag AutoSwitch KVM into Applications. The first launch is blocked
          (no paid Apple certificate yet): go to <strong>System Settings ▸ Privacy &amp; Security</strong>
          and click <strong>Open Anyway</strong>. Then allow Bluetooth when it asks.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="dl">
        <h3>Windows</h3>
        <p class="dl__req">Windows 10 (1809+) or 11 · x64 · <a href="{{ site.download.windowsArm }}">ARM64 here</a></p>
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="{{ site.download.windows }}">
          <svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0-5-5m5 5 5-5M5 21h14"/></svg>
          Download for Windows
        </a>
        <p class="dl__note">
          Run the installer, no admin needed. If SmartScreen says "Windows protected your PC",
          click <strong>More info ▸ Run anyway</strong> (same story: no paid certificate yet).
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="downloads__more">Every version and its release notes are on <a href="{{ site.releases }}">GitHub Releases</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- FAQ ---------- #}
<section class="section" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <div class="section__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
      <h2>Good to know</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need it on both computers?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes. A Magic Trackpad can only be paired with one computer at a time, so the computer
          you're leaving has to let go before the other one can pair. Each copy handles its own
          side of that handoff.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Will it work with my KVM switch?</summary>
        <p>
          Very likely. It works with any KVM that switches USB between the computers, which is how
          almost all of them share your keyboard and mouse. AutoSwitch watches for the USB device
          (usually a hub inside the KVM) that appears and disappears with each switch.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Which Bluetooth devices work?</summary>
        <p>
          Apple Magic Trackpad, Keyboard and Mouse; Logitech Easy-Switch keyboards and mice like the
          K380; ZMK keyboards with the <a href="https://github.com/casab/zmk-autoswitch">zmk-autoswitch</a>
          module; and most headphones and speakers. Game controllers can't be switched by any app;
          AutoSwitch tells you so when you add one. <a href="/devices/">The device guide</a> has the details.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why does a switch take a few seconds?</summary>
        <p>
          The computer you switched to has to wait until the other one lets go of the device, and
          Bluetooth pairing itself takes a moment. AutoSwitch retries quietly until the device is
          free, so you don't have to.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does it collect any data?</summary>
        <p>
          No. There's no account and no analytics. Your settings stay on your computer. The app only
          contacts GitHub to check for updates.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is it really free?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes. The source code is on <a href="{{ site.github }}">GitHub</a>. Found a bug or have
          an idea? <a href="{{ site.issues }}">Open an issue</a>.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ---------- Final call ---------- #}
<section class="finale">
  <div class="wrap finale__inner">
    <h2>Go on. Switch something.</h2>
    <a class="btn btn--big" href="#download">Get AutoSwitch KVM</a>
  </div>
</section>
